## Security and Performance Anti-Patterns

### Security Anti-Patterns to Avoid
- ❌ Storing sensitive data in client-side storage
- ❌ Exposing API keys or secrets in client code
- ❌ Not validating user inputs on the server side
- ❌ Using weak authentication mechanisms
- ❌ Not implementing proper authorization checks
- ❌ Trusting client-side data without validation
- ❌ Not implementing rate limiting
- ❌ Using outdated dependencies with known vulnerabilities

### Performance Anti-Patterns to Avoid
- ❌ Loading unnecessary data or large payloads
- ❌ Not implementing proper caching strategies
- ❌ Creating unnecessary re-renders in React
- ❌ Not optimizing images and media assets
- ❌ Blocking the main thread with expensive operations
- ❌ Not implementing proper error boundaries
- ❌ Using inefficient database queries
- ❌ Not monitoring and profiling application performance
